But wait — when the service runs `this.prisma.$transaction([this.prisma.bookmark.updateMany({...}), this.prisma.collection.delete({...})])`, the arguments to `$transaction` are evaluated first (JavaScript evaluates arguments left-to-right before calling the function). So `mockPrisma.bookmark.updateMany` IS called before `mockPrisma.collection.delete` because they're in array position 0 and 1 respectively.

